+/**
+ * A successful profile write (avatar included) is the authoritative identity for
+ * this user, but the mounted rosters are membership snapshots: the server roster
+ * still holds the pre-write row, and channel message rows resolve their sender
+ * avatar from the channel roster, which is only re-read on membership events. A
+ * profile edit from Settings or the member panel would therefore leave the old
+ * avatar in an already-open channel until a reload. Re-read the server roster and
+ * invalidate every channel roster so both stores converge on the written identity.
+ *
+ * Best-effort by design: the write already succeeded, so a roster refresh must
+ * never turn a successful avatar/profile update into a rejected action.
+ * `loadMembers` already records its own failure in `membersLoadError`, and
+ * channel listeners re-read independently.
+ */
+function refreshMemberRostersAfterProfileWrite(): void {
+  void useServerStore.getState().loadMembers().catch(() => {
+    // The write is authoritative; the roster will be re-read by the next event.
+  });
+  notifyAllChannelMembersChanged();
+}
